@*
    The dialog that Blazor shows while the connection to the server is lost (MIL-033). Without an element with this
    id, blazor.web.js injects its own dialog with an inline style, which the Content Security Policy refuses
    (style-src 'self'). With it, Blazor only sets one of the classes components-reconnect-show, -failed, -rejected
    or -hide on the element, and app.css shows the matching text. The reload link is a plain link to the page,
    not a javascript: link, which the policy refuses too.
*@

<div id="components-reconnect-modal" class="reconnect" role="alert" aria-live="assertive">
    <div class="reconnect-box">
        <p class="reconnect-text reconnect-text-show">Forbindelsen til serveren er afbrudt. Prøver igen …</p>
        <p class="reconnect-text reconnect-text-failed">Forbindelsen kunne ikke genoprettes.</p>
        <p class="reconnect-text reconnect-text-rejected">Sessionen er udløbet.</p>
        <a class="reconnect-reload" href="">Genindlæs siden</a>
    </div>
</div>
